{"title":"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A gallon of paint is used to paint a room. One third of the paint is used on the first day. On the second day, one third of the remaining paint is used. What fraction of the original amount of paint is available to use on the third day?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0ba0ca373308de801b689211a795cc68ab848a29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{1}{10} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\frac{1}{9} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\frac{4}{9} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\frac{5}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"384\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After the first day, there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/b/48b262b6d4eab460fa3ba443162cc38243c1a8c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\left(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\cdot1\\right)=\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"132\" height=\"45\" /> gallons left. After the second day, there is a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f98128e02b6d4d069b975edbf97183e8707009ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{2}{3}-\\left(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\times\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right)=\\dfrac{2}{3}-\\dfrac{2}{9}=\\dfrac{4}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"218\" height=\"43\" />. Therefore, the fraction of the original amount of paint that is left is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b58d1d908613ef43bf08ef810eaf4ef016c80ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\dfrac{4}{9}}{1}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{4}{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"103\" height=\"63\" />.\n</p><p>Another way to do this is just to simply find the gain everyday and subtract from the remaining you had before.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B\">2005 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/